---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ClockSampler from '../components/ClockSampler.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import { LICENSES } from '../data/licenses';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { CLOCKS, clockSources } from '../data/clocks';
import { STATES } from '../data/states';
import { homeFaqs } from '../lib/faqs';

const cited = CLOCKS.length;
const pages = STATES.length * LICENSES.length;
const texas = CLOCKS.find((c) => c.state === 'TX' && c.license === 'money-transmitter')!;
const texasSource = clockSources(texas)[0];
const texasState = STATES.find((s) => s.code === 'TX')!;
const texasLicense = LICENSES.find((l) => l.id === 'money-transmitter')!;

const faqs = homeFaqs(cited);

const proof = CLOCKS.map((clock) => {
  const state = STATES.find((s) => s.code === clock.state)!;
  const license = LICENSES.find((l) => l.id === clock.license)!;
  const source = clockSources(clock)[0];
  return { clock, state, license, source };
});
---

<Layout
  title={`${SITE.name} | Cited timelines for U.S. business licensing`}
  description="Cited statutory clocks and regulator-published waits for U.S. collection, lending, money transmitter, and mortgage company licenses. A typical range stays blank when it is not published."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Cited U.S. licensing timelines</p>
          <h1>See the cited clock before you set a launch date.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            For operators sequencing collection, consumer lending, money transmission, and mortgage
            company filings. Fifty states. A figure appears when a statute or a regulator page publishes it.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn btn-solid" href={SITE.cornerstone.contact} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ask Cornerstone</a>
            <a class="text-cta" href="#sampler">Read a cited clock</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <article class="ledger" aria-label="Texas money transmitter statutory clock">
          <p class="kicker">{texas.state} · {texasLicense.shortName}</p>
          <p class="figure">{texas.days}<span>days</span></p>
          <h2>{texas.label}</h2>
          <p>
            Statutory clock. Deemed approval if the agency is silent. The period may be extended for good cause.
            Clock starts: {texas.clockStarts}.
          </p>
          <p class="meta" style="margin-top:14px">
            <a href={texasSource.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{texasSource.title}</a>
            <br />
            <a href={`/licenses/${texasLicense.slug}/${texasState.slug}/`}>Open the Texas page</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <ul class="fact-row">
        <li><strong>{pages}</strong><span>state × license pages</span></li>
        <li><strong>{cited}</strong><span>cited clocks in this build</span></li>
        <li><strong>4</strong><span>cores Cornerstone files</span></li>
        <li><strong>{SITE.accessed}</strong><span>sources accessed</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-rule" id="problem">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="kicker">The problem</p>
        <h2>The date on the slide is usually ahead of the file.</h2>
        <p>
          A launch calendar is only as sturdy as the clock underneath it. These are the three places
          that clock gets misread.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-grid">
        <article>
          <span class="index-no">01</span>
          <h3>Completeness starts the statute.</h3>
          <p>
            The statutory windows in this directory start when the agency treats the application as
            complete, not the hour someone clicks submit. A deficiency letter is how most long waits begin.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="index-no">02</span>
          <h3>A deadline and an average are different.</h3>
          <p>
            A 120-day money-transmitter statute is a decision deadline after completeness. Several of
            those statutes allow an extension for good cause. Silence counts as approval only where the cited section says so.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="index-no">03</span>
          <h3>Unpublished means the cell stays blank.</h3>
          <p>
            Most of the {pages} pair pages have no regulator-published typical range. The blank is
            deliberate, so a planning number has to come from a source you can open.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-rule" id="sampler">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="kicker">The directory</p>
        <h2>Pick a state and a core. Read what is cited.</h2>
        <p>
          Six clocks have a statute or a regulator-published timeframe. Every other pair resolves to
          “typical range unknown,” with the regulator desk named on the full page.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ClockSampler />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-rule" id="proof">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="kicker">Proof</p>
        <h2>Six clocks, each tied to a public source.</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing else in the directory is given a number. California’s three-week figure is an
          individual MLO endorsement window, kept adjacent to the company license.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-grid">
        {
          proof.map(({ clock, state, license, source }) => (
            <a class="tile" href={`/licenses/${license.slug}/${state.slug}/`}>
              <p class="meta">
                {state.name} · {license.shortName}
                {clock.adjacent ? ' · adjacent' : ''}
              </p>
              {clock.days && (
                <p class="figure proof-figure">
                  {clock.days}
                  <span>days</span>
                </p>
              )}
              <h3>{clock.kind === 'statutory' ? 'Statutory clock' : 'Regulator-published'}</h3>
              <p>{clock.label}</p>
              <p class="meta" style="margin-top:10px">{source.publisher}</p>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-rule" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="kicker">How the desk is used</p>
        <h2>Read the pair. Then ask for a real calendar.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <span class="index-no">01</span>
          <strong>Open the state and the core.</strong>
          Collection, consumer lending, money transmitter, or mortgage company: one page per state.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="index-no">02</span>
          <strong>Separate the clock from the wait.</strong>
          A statutory outer bound, a regulator-published window, or a blank. NMLS stays the filing channel. The state keeps the review clock.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="index-no">03</span>
          <strong>Ask Cornerstone to sequence the file.</strong>
          The operating partner prepares and files. This directory keeps the citations.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="sister-grid">
        <a class="tile" href="/licenses/">
          <p class="meta">This desk</p>
          <h3>How long</h3>
          <p>Cited clocks, the delays that stop them, and when an expedite is actually published.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="tile" href={SITE.sisters.simple.url}>
          <p class="meta">{SITE.sisters.simple.name}</p>
          <h3>Who files, and where</h3>
          <p>{SITE.sisters.simple.job}.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="tile" href={SITE.sisters.store.url}>
          <p class="meta">{SITE.sisters.store.name}</p>
          <h3>What it costs</h3>
          <p>{SITE.sisters.store.job}.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="link-row">
        <a href="/guides/how-long-does-a-business-license-take/">How long a business license takes</a>
        <a href="/delays/">What delays a file</a>
        <a href="/expedite/">When an expedite is published</a>
        <a href="/methodology/">How a figure earns a place</a>
        <a href="/about/">Who keeps the desk</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-rule" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="kicker">FAQ</p>
        <h2>Before the date goes on a slide.</h2>
      </div>
      <FaqList items={faqs} />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
